    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0229" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.35112RP/2–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-14T18:00:00-03:00">February 14, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 14—5:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>484. Re Embassy’s telegram 426, February 8, 7 p.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d178-f1"
                    /> Appellate Court yesterday rejected Judge Ortiz Basualdo’s order restraining
                    Junta de Vigilancia from taking possession of Staudt firms.<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d178-f2"/></p>
                <p>Without deciding constitutional question, Court held order was unjustified
                    judicial interference with the executive functions required to fulfill
                    obligations under Chapultepec and United Nations pacts and that measures placing
                    Staudt firms under Junta’s control were in compliance with international
                    agreements which are incorporate in Argentine legislation.</p>
                <p>It is believed certain that Staudt will petition for review by Supreme
                        Court<anchor n="64" xml:id="d178-f3"/> in which case Junta cannot proceed to
                    take possession until Supreme Court either denies petition to review or affirms
                    Appellate Court.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d178-f1" n="62" xml:id="d178-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d178-f2" n="63" xml:id="d178-f2-content">
                <p>German firms appearing on the Proclaimed List and object of court action in Chile
                    as well as Argentina.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d178-f3" n="64" xml:id="d178-f3-content">
                <p>For action of this court, see telegram 1858, July 18, from Buenos Aires, <ref
                        target="#pg280">p. 280</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
